# BMAD-generated content — installer output from `bmad install`.
# Keep byte-identical to what the installer produces so re-running it yields no
# spurious diff. Never reformat these. Team/personal config in _bmad/custom/ and
# your own (non-bmad-) skills/agents are NOT ignored and format normally.
_bmad/
.claude/skills/bmad-*/
.agents/skills/bmad-*/
.github/agents/bmad-*
.github/copilot-instructions.md

# Claude Code worktrees: full checkouts of this repo nested inside it.
# git excludes them via .git/info/exclude, which is local-only and NOT something
# prettier can read (it honours .gitignore and .prettierignore, nothing else), so
# without this entry prettier walks every worktree. Two consequences, both real:
# `prettier --check .` goes from ~11s to over six minutes (239k extra files), and
# `yarn format` would rewrite files inside other in-flight branches.
.claude/worktrees/

# Written by `expo prebuild` back into the tracked source tree.
# @bacons/apple-targets' watch-icon mod writes this file itself, via
# writeContentsJsonAsync -> JSON.stringify(…, null, 2) with NO trailing newline
# (@expo/prebuild-config/build/plugins/icons/AssetContents.js). Prettier wants to
# add that newline. The two can never agree, so whichever tool writes last, the
# other reports the file as modified -- which is why `yarn watch:prebuild` used to
# leave a stray one-byte diff in `git status` for a file nobody touched.
# prebuild is the generator of record here, so keep prettier (and, via this file,
# lint-staged) out of it and let the tracked bytes match prebuild exactly.
targets/watch/Assets.xcassets/AppIcon.appiconset/Contents.json

# Room's exported schema JSON (Story 10.5), generated by the Room compiler + the Room Gradle plugin
# (`room { schemaDirectory(...) }` in watch-android/app/build.gradle.kts) and committed so migrations
# can be diffed per version. Room is the generator of record: it re-emits this file on every build in
# its own formatting, so prettier reformatting it would guarantee a spurious diff on the next build —
# the same generated-artifact situation as tokens.generated.ts and the AppIcon Contents.json above.
# Keep prettier out of it and let the committed bytes match Room's output exactly.
watch-android/app/schemas/

# Hand-tuned HTML, deliberately left as authored.
# docs/ is served publicly by GitHub Pages (https://ifero.github.io/myLoyaltyCards/,
# source main:/docs) and supabase/templates/ are the transactional auth emails.
# Prettier's HTML printer explodes every inline style="…" attribute across multiple
# lines and reflows inline elements: ~1.2k lines of churn, no functional gain, and
# multi-line attributes are exactly what older email clients mishandle. All risk,
# no upside. Sibling CSS is NOT ignored -- prettier's CSS output is safe.
docs/*.html
supabase/templates/*.html

# Design-exploration artifacts kept as authored records, not as maintained source.
# palette-bench.html is a single self-contained comparison board emitted by a Claude
# Artifact: ~45k of inlined CSS and SVG specimens whose exact bytes are the record of
# what the room actually judged. Reformatting it would churn the whole file and prove
# nothing, and nothing builds from it — same generated-artifact case as the docs/ HTML.
docs/design/cardi/*.html

# The design frames, and their generators of record in docs/design/cardi/tools/.
# The entry above uses a single `*`, which does not cross a directory separator, so
# frames/ was never covered by it. These files are BUILT -- `python3 tools/verify.py`
# asserts that every generator still reproduces its frame byte for byte, which is the
# guard against a stale generator silently reverting a hand fix. Prettier reformatting
# the committed output would break that check permanently and for no gain, so the
# generators stay the source of truth here. Same case as the Room schemas above.
docs/design/cardi/frames/*.html
